    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #358\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-147-system-i18n-05-05-localize-api-and-age-thr_pvk76vsc8d` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nCloses #147 (\"[system-i18n 05/05] Localize API and agent-manifest projections\").\n\n`generatePermissionManifest` (`backend/packages/data/src/manifest/permissionManifest.ts`) now accepts an optional `{ moduleRegistry, locale }` and resolves database names, property names, and select/multi_select option labels through the `resolveCatalogLabel` fallback chain (explicit stored override → requested locale → English → raw key). A database's `owner_module_id` column stores the database *key*, not the owning `ModuleManifest.id`, so the resolver first builds a `key -> moduleId` map from `ModuleRegistry.getDatabases()` before loading catalogs — getting this wrong would have silently resolved nothing. `createDriftCheckAction` threads the same options through so its resolvability check also validates catalog resolution when a registry is supplied. Callers that omit `moduleRegistry` (every existing call site) keep the exact pre-#147 raw-key placeholder behavior, so nothing regresses.\n\nNo live HTTP endpoint currently serializes databases/properties/options/agent-tools (confirmed `routeMatrix.ts` is exhaustive), so this issue's \"API response serializers\" requirement is delivered as the shared, reusable resolver wired into the one real projection that exists today (the AGENT.md manifest), ready for a future endpoint to reuse without further resolver work.\n\nNew integration tests cover: cs/en catalog resolution for a system database's name, a property's name, and select-option labels; English fallback; raw-key fallback when no registry is given; explicit overrides winning over the catalog in every locale; and byte-for-byte preservation of user-authored (non-system) database names.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `pnpm run test:unit` — 18 files, 127 tests pass\n- [x] `pnpm run test:integration` — 68 files, 794 tests pass\n- [x] `pnpm run test:e2e` — 1 file, 5 tests pass\n- [x] `pnpm run lint` — clean\n- [x] `pnpm run check:boundaries` — clean (378 modules, 1752 dependencies)\n- [x] `tsc --noEmit` on `packages/data` and `packages/module-registry` — clean\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
