    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #358\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nWorking tree had no remaining changes to commit. Pushed the new commit to the existing branch `bb/relay-147-system-i18n-05-05-localize-api-and-age-thr_pvk76vsc8d` on origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis push addresses the third round of AI Code Review feedback on PR #358 for issue #147:\n\n- **AC #9/#10 (blocking)**: `driftCheck.ts`, the only production caller of `generatePermissionManifest`, now resolves a real `users.locale` live on every heartbeat run instead of always passing `undefined`. Since Semprec has no owning-user column on projects/databases (single-tenant), the earliest-created account is used as the honest stand-in for \"the\" user; a new `getEarliestUserLocale` helper backs this. The lookup happens inside the same transaction each run, so a locale change is reflected on the very next tick with nothing persisted to go stale.\n- **Low**: `schemaHandler.ts`'s 405 response now includes the `Allow: GET` header required by RFC 7231 §6.5.5.\n- Deduplicated the `users.locale` → `ManifestLocale` narrowing helper into `catalogResolution.ts`, shared by both the API handler and the drift check.\n\nAll checks pass: unit (127/127), integration (808/808), e2e (5/5), lint, format, and dependency-boundary checks are all clean.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
